  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 and takes about 50 minutes."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Miso"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ramen is the boldest and most substantial of the classic styles. The"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "tare"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "here is built on miso paste, which gives the broth its characteristic depth without needing hours of simmering. The"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "noodle-ramen"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "holds up well in the thicker broth, staying springy all the way to the last bite."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Never boil the broth after adding the miso tare. Boiling miso drives off its aroma and turns the broth bitter. Stir the tare into each bowl first, then ladle the hot broth over it. This is the same principle as the shio version. Individual seasoning in each bowl gives you precise control."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
